Keep the linker start function in Emscripten mode

With shared memory (`-pthread`), wasm-ld makes the data segments passive and
puts `__wasm_init_memory`, which initializes them, into the start section.
wasm-bindgen moves every start function to the export `__wbindgen_start`
(`unstart_start_function()` in `src/transforms/mod.rs`), which its JavaScript
calls after instantiation, so the data segments are no longer initialized when
the module is instantiated. emcc reads the strings of `EM_JS` and `EM_ASM` code
from the data segments through that start function; for a module that has such
strings (for example with `-sMALLOC=mimalloc`) it fails in
`tools/extract_metadata.py`, `get_passive_segment_offsets()`, with
`assert start_func_index is not None`. In Emscripten mode this patch takes the
linker start function aside before processing and puts it back into the start
section at the end; only the start code of wasm-bindgen goes to
`__wbindgen_start`. Single-threaded modules have no start function, so the
patch changes nothing for them.

Upstream has no issue and no fix for this defect.

On a version bump: the patch must apply without fuzz, and a threaded
Emscripten module (`-pthread`, `-sMALLOC=mimalloc`, Rust std built with
`+atomics`) must link with the patched CLI and keep its start section.

--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -417,6 +417,23 @@
             bail!("--experimental-reset-state-function is only supported for --target module, --target web, or --target nodejs")
         }
 
+        // With shared memory, wasm-ld makes the data segments passive and
+        // initializes them in a start function. Emscripten runs that start
+        // function at instantiation on every thread and reads the segments
+        // through it, so it must stay in the start section; only the start
+        // code that wasm-bindgen adds moves to `__wbindgen_start`. The
+        // temporary export keeps the function alive meanwhile; its name must
+        // not start with `__wbindgen`, because `unexport_intrinsics()` deletes
+        // those exports.
+        let linker_start = if self.mode.emscripten() {
+            module.start.take().map(|id| {
+                module.exports.add("__binarylandia_linker_start", id);
+                id
+            })
+        } else {
+            None
+        };
+
         let thread_count = if self.mode.emscripten() {
             // Emscripten owns multithreading bootstrap logic.
             None
@@ -594,6 +611,21 @@
             emscripten_extern_pre_js,
         };
 
+        if let Some(id) = linker_start {
+            let export = module
+                .exports
+                .iter()
+                .find(|export| export.name == "__binarylandia_linker_start")
+                .map(walrus::Export::id);
+            if let Some(export) = export {
+                module.exports.delete(export);
+            }
+            if !module.funcs.iter().any(|func| func.id() == id) {
+                bail!("the linker start function was removed");
+            }
+            module.start = Some(id);
+        }
+
